     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and 1,700 mg is also above the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day in total.** This could be 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** Tell me the dose and frequency you want.\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and I'll enter it with a note recording that the dose was verified. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
